ENT 3D upper-body meshes

skull.glb and auricle.glb are a decimated extract of the Z-Anatomy Blender
template (Startup.blend), which is Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International.

Checked 2026-11-21:
- https://github.com/LluisV/Z-Anatomy LICENSE is CC BY-SA 4.0
- https://github.com/Z-Anatomy/Models-of-human-anatomy License.txt is CC BY-SA 4.0
  and requires attribution to BodyParts3D (CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan) and Z-Anatomy

Included, right and left where the template has both:
frontal, parietal, occipital, sphenoid, temporal, mandible, maxilla,
zygomatic, nasal, ethmoid, vomer, lacrimal, inferior nasal concha, hyoid,
atlas, axis, C3–C7, clavicles, and the right auricle cartilage parts
(helix, antihelix, crura, tragus, antitragus, lobule, concha, cymba, cavum).

The Integument collection and the External ear collection in that template
contain no mesh. There is no skin surface to export. The auricle here is the
cartilage parts, not a skin envelope.

The extract was decimated, rigidly mapped into the OpenEar ZETA millimetre
frame (+X anterior, +Y inferior, +Z medial), and translated so the right
ear-canal estimate meets the ZETA canal. Scale is 1.0. A mastoid-tip match
would have needed a scale of about 0.75, outside the 5% band, so it was not
applied. That registration is unverified.

Changes: decimation, unit conversion from metres, axis remap, translation.
